tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert/usage/profiles
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert/usage/profiles/normalize
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Optional.  A list of steps that reshape the source document before the records
path is resolved.  Everything downstream — bindings, the shape trees, the field
picker — sees the reshaped document.

One step exists, `pivot`.  It turns an array of entry-objects into the object
those entries describe, which is what you need when a source reports each field
as `{"key": "date", "value": "9/16/26", "type": "string"}` rather than as
`"date": "9/16/26"`:

```
"normalize": [{"pivot": {}}]
```

With no options, pivot rewrites every array in the document whose elements all
carry both a `key` and a `value` property; anything else is left alone.  Values
are copied across unchanged, so numbers stay numbers and transforms still apply.
Duplicate keys within one group resolve last-wins, with a warning, and a step
that matches nothing raises `normalize-no-effect`.

|!Option  |!Default    |!Meaning                                            |
|`key`    |`"key"`     |Property holding the field name                     |
|`value`  |`"value"`   |Property holding the field value                    |
|`at`     |whole document |Path limiting the rewrite (`[*]` allowed, `..` not) |

The Console's ''Flatten key/value pair arrays'' checkbox writes and removes the
default step for you, and the profile editor has the same checkbox above the
records path.  Hand-written options survive editing either way.
